* ''Engine cadence'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Cadence keeps its own lineage and threshold, apart from every seat key. A Nexus's joint founding cites one cadence inception that names each founder's hearth, the device that bears the reboot, as a holder; a household seed carries none, since its one holder bears its reboots. Each hearth mints its cadence key at random on the device, never derived from serving or floor material, and keeps it, with its next-key commitment, as a `cold` record under the vessel key that unwraps per act; no sixth custody class and no extra card at the founding. A holder may later rotate onto a cold card by its own choice. Each island pins one engine epoch, and one daemon hosts two epochs only as two separately pinned islands. The reason: the people who bear a reboot decide it, and a seat-holder who runs no hardware forces no one's restart. The ruling flips on a cadence act that must run unattended where a per-act unwrap cannot (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract`>>).

